  "explanation": {
    "en": "〜歳 (さい) is the counter for age. It is used to say how old someone is. The age 20 has a special reading: はたち.\n\nKey points:\n• Use number + 歳 to state age\n• 20 years old = はたち (special)\n• Question: 何歳ですか (How old?)\n• Polite: おいくつですか (more polite)\n\nExample: “私は二十歳です” means “I am 20 years old.” “何歳ですか” means “How old are you?”\n\nThe reading さい is regular for most numbers. Remember the special form はたち for 20.\n\nPractice by stating ages: 十八歳, 二十二歳, 三十歳.",
    "ja": ""
  },
